The year of Superluminal on the Linux desktop is finally here. It has been a huge undertaking, and the team is excited to release it to the wild. They are curious to see how well it works outside their small group and encourage others to try it.

@SuperluminalSft: "We're finally bringing our powerful and user-friendly CPU profiler to Linux. The beta version is now publicly available, and it's free for 60 days during the open beta, so there's really no excuse not to try it out. Just download, extract, and optimize."

The profiler is an industry-leading sampling tool that displays profiling data visually, aiming to simplify CPU performance analysis on Linux systems.
